# Source Notes Template

This template defines the footer that should appear at the end of every
learning module (concept files, daily sessions, etc.).

## Footer Format

```markdown
---

### Source Notes
- [source 1 description] - [verified] or [unverified]
- [source 2 description] - [verified] or [unverified]

### Material Sources
- Material ID: {M001}; Location: {page / slide / section / location unresolved}; Coverage: Grounded / Partially grounded

### Supplemental Sources
- {supplemental source or "None"} - reason: {why supplemental content was needed}

### Unresolved Extraction Issues
- {issue ID or "None"} - impact: {what content may be incomplete}

### Freshness Risk: 🟢 Stable / 🟡 Evolving / 🔴 Volatile

### Claims to Verify
- [ ] {claim 1} - suggested verification: {method}
- [ ] {claim 2} - suggested verification: {method}

**Last Verified**: {date or "not yet verified"}
**Recommended Review Interval**: {interval}
```

## Usage

The AI agent appends this footer to every learning module it generates.
The learner can use the "Claims to Verify" checklist to independently
confirm key facts.

In Material-Grounded Learning Mode, Source Notes must separate user material
from `Supplemental` sources. Do not hide outside knowledge under Material
Sources.

If the agent has no web access, add this notice at the top of the module:

```markdown
> [!WARNING]
> **Unverified Draft**
>
> This content was generated without web access. Key claims must be verified
> against authoritative sources before use.
```
